# K03 NS-ROLES-V2 (the author, 2026-10-07; docs #declaration-visibility): a callable fn, fm or sub creates is
# visible both ways within its lexical block -- a method's own fn in its method's body, above its definition too --
# and nowhere outside that block; ordinary data and a receiver's output only from their place on.
# The same from a block nested in makeAdder's body (an if), above addN's definition.  Exit 7 when both calls
# ran.
int: hits 0
fn: makeAdder (int: n) fn: (int: x) int
    int: t 0
    if: n > 0
        t: addN(1)
    node\hits: node\hits + t
    fn: addN (int: x) int
        return: n + x
    return: addN
fn: check (int: v) int
    return: v + node\hits - 6
@: add5 makeAdder(5)
sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(add5(2)); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
